  "description": "Pure-managed TLS 1.3 (RFC 8446) for .NET — client and server, sync and async, with no BCrypt/OpenSSL P/Invoke (a single BCryptGenRandom entropy import remains). Includes the X25519MLKEM768, SecP256r1MLKEM768 and SecP384r1MLKEM1024 hybrid post-quantum key exchanges (FIPS 203 ML-KEM-768 and ML-KEM-1024, per draft-ietf-tls-ecdhe-mlkem), mTLS (with RFC 8879 client-certificate compression), PSK resumption, 0-RTT early data, HelloRetryRequest, ALPN, OCSP stapling, Encrypted Client Hello (draft-ietf-tls-esni-18 — incl. accept-confirmation, outer_extensions compression, GREASE and retry_configs), certificate compression (RFC 8879: zlib/brotli/zstd), and the GOST (RFC 9367) and Chinese SM (RFC 8998) national cipher suites. NativeAOT-friendly; zero transitive dependencies (all crypto is source-vendored).",
